1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,020
Everyone knows Atlantis, but almost no one
knows where the story actually comes from.

2
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:10,500
There is no ancient map, no ruins, no
inscription.

3
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:14,720
The entire legend comes from one man,
Plato.

4
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:21,180
Around 360 BC, he wrote it into two
dialogues, the Timaeus and the Critias.

5
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:25,040
And the story he tells is a chain of
whispers.

6
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:29,160
An Egyptian priest told it to the Athenian
statesman Solon.

7
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:35,190
Solon passed it on, and it was handed
down, generation after generation,

8
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:37,800
until it reached Plato's character,
Critias.

9
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:43,610
The priest spoke of a mighty naval empire
beyond the Pillars of Hercules,

10
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:46,320
an empire that tried to conquer the
Mediterranean.

11
00:00:46,780 --> 00:00:52,860
Then, in a single day and night, earthquakes
and floods swallowed it into the sea.

12
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:54,200
When did this happen?

13
00:00:54,360 --> 00:01:00,300
9,000 years before Plato, yet no writer
before him ever mentions it.

14
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:06,020
Many historians believe Plato invented it
as a warning about arrogant empires.

15
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:10,520
So, was Atlantis real, or the greatest
story ever told?
